<title>BRAZIL: Venezuela may hike public wages 25 pct in 1997.</title>
<headline>Venezuela may hike public wages 25 pct in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan Planning Minister Teodoro Petkoff said Thursday Caracas expected a wage hike for public sector servants next year of about 25 percent.</p>
<p>Petkoff told Reuters during a visit to the Brazilian capital Brasilia that speculation about indexation was out of place.</p>
<p>&quot;The government is not considering indexing wages. We think indexation is pernicious,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;What there is is the expectation...that a wage increase for the public sector based on the expected inflation for 1997 will be approved so it comes into effect on January 1, 1997.&quot;  </p>
<p>Petkoff added that the government expected inflation to reach about 25 percent next year.</p>
<p>Asked if therefore a 25 percent wage hike for all public sector servants was in the cards in 1997, he said, &quot;Yes.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
</text>
